1|0@wow^1440601097#cugawye:LongLastingStick$:I mostly only play priest and warrior so - Warrior: Arms is really boring. I'd like to see overpower come back in some form and take whirlwind out of the rotation. I like arms as being the big single hits and the cleaving. The berserker identity is already in fury, and Arms spec identity should be closer to a battle master / champion sorta deal. Fury I don't play so no opinion. I don't think protection really needs that much changed. It's not a super complicated spec, but I've always enjoyed it. I'd like to see gladiator get a little boost to dps, but I think it'd need a lot of work to flesh out into a real dps alternative. What would really get my juices flowing would be renaming it "myrmidon" and giving the ability to wield spears + shields. I'd like to see some tweaks to protection survivability namely rework shield barrier to be an actual spell damage stopper or a shield on par with other tanks absorbs and another self survivability cooldown. Priest: I recently respecced out of shadow, so my opinion there isn't as thorough. I'd like to see the CoP style go away and instead stick to the DoTs - CoP comes out of nowhere at 100 and basically replaces the leveling rotation. Refocusing on dots, I also think shadow needs a flavor revamp: there are lots of cool shadow effects to choose from in WoD and shadow still has the lame visuals it's had for a while. Devouring plague should be reworked into something more theme appropriate - the name made sense when it was an undead spell but it should be something more shadowy now. The spec could also use some better cool downs. Disc they're already changing, so kinda just need to wait and see. I'm hoping it ends up being something closer to a mistweaver. Imo the way shields have been used since wrath is bad design and should be reworked for the overall health of the healing game. Holy needs a numbers boost more than anything else. The spec has plenty of tools and is pretty fun to play, but it's got shitty tier bonuses, beyond shit trinket, and low numbers. Those are fixable without reworking the spec too much. One thing that would be cool is replacing the mastery with an amp instead of a hot, and you wouldn't even need to change the name - "Echo of Light: increases healing received by x for y seconds". Even if it only applies to the caster, it'd be a nice different mastery than the hot which doesn't always work that well. I would also like to see spirit of redemption reworked into a cool down a la ascension, the current iteration is rarely useful but the effect is cool. In general with priest healing specs I'd like to get a damage boost. I run holy / disc and trying to kill anything is a drag. I'd be down with changing red chakra to increase damage a further 20% but reduce healing done by 20%. Also extend the dot effect of holy fire to better benefit the smite glyph. Disc / holy also really needs a new damage spell - holy Paladins have a bunch of holy damage spells and can pull together a passable solo spec while priests are stuck either spamming holy fire + smite or holy fire + penance + smite. 
