1|0@wow^1440597697#cug8umg:mikally$:I would have been fine with no demon hunters and a 4th spec for every class minus druids. I would have also like to see a 3rd alternate talent set become available. I think it would have added some diversity to familiar classes. I think the pure dps classes would have benefited the most from something like this. You could add either a tank or healing spec to all classes with 3 dps specs. I believe it would help with the tank/healer imbalance, particularly in pug/LFR crowds. No class would be permanently stuck with a 40 minute q time because they can't do anything but dps. It would add a level of gameplay that we haven't seen in a long, long time. Rogues could get a tank spec. Mages could get a healing spec. Warlocks and shamans could have gotten a tanking spec finally; instead the idea of demonic form tanking just got hijacked by the 2 spec hero class. Hunters could have gone either way honestly, I think the idea of something like healing shots/darts would be cool though. Priests/Paladins/Monks/DK's could have a 2nd/3rd dps option. Warriors could have a stand alone gladiator stance spec. Druids would be druids. I think a 4th spec would have been a better way to spend development time. Demon hunters will be cool, but not everyone can main one. One of the major defining points of this expansion will be players favorite alt at best. A 4th spec would have been something everyone could have gotten behind. Artifact weapons are a cool idea on an individual level. There are a lot of mixed feelings on legendaries for everyone already without those items being major lore weapons. Just my opinion though. Legion will be alright I'm sure. I'm ready to see who dies(Thrall) /gives up that leads us to our lore weapons. Also a 4th spec isn't something that had to be done this expansion. I would be excited to see that feature in a future expansion. 
