1|0@wow^1440592270#cug690p:daemonicBookkeeper$:**Mages**: Delete Rune of Power. Rune of Power exacerbates mobility issues (especially with Arcane) and encourages players to ignore raid mechanics in order to continue DPSing. It's only the mathematically superior talent to make up for how horrible it is to play with. Fire: Many fun things about this spec have slowly dissolved over the years. Fiery Payback, Impact (next fire blast version), Blast Wave knockback, Combustion stun/copies all dots, Ignite on crits (while less consistent, much more fun). Fire is the crit spec. Make it crit way, way more than other specs. Mastery ignite is dumb and Combustion's ten million redesigns don't help. Reinforce Fire's strongest themes from WoW history: - Critical hits and bonuses for them - Dangerous when cornered (in short range with high damage short range spells, at low health with Fiery Payback) - Defensive style based on bursts of movement and short duration hard cc like Dragon's Breath and Impact, rather than the methodical kiting and constant slows of Frost Blazing Speed into the boss to use Dragon's Breath is *good, fun gameplay*. Yes, you might then be stuck in fire with no mobility skill, but you still have Blink and besides, that's what knowing the encounter is for. Make Combustion more satisfying to use; its only current effect is a lame sound effect and a bump on the dps meters, and the fact that it resets Inferno Blast is way more cool and interesting than anything the spell actually does. Make self-cast Blast Waves knock back enemies if you insist on replacing Frost Nova with it. **Warlocks**: Pets are still a pain in the ass over 10 years in. If you want "the average warlock to have a pet out" then a) don't make Grimoire of Sacrifice the best talent and b) don't make pets despawn so frequently. Rode my Goblin Glider? No pet. Pet got distracted by a mob I left 80 yards behind? No pet. Destruction: I miss Chaos Bolt being a zippy spell with a short cast time, fast projectile and still sick damage. And it pierced shields too! Enemies will routinely die before Chaos Bolt reaches them, and a "burst phase" consisting of Dark Soul into 4x Chaos Bolt is exceedingly slow and vulnerable to raid mechanics like fire or knockups, not to mention not very engaging. Embers are cool but Ember Tap is really anemic (7% hp?); Flames of Xoroth is not a replacement for Health Funnel; and Fire and Brimstone, while excellent, is frustrating to use on packs of minor enemies since your entire AoE spell is cancelled by a primary target dying. Rain of Fire is anemic to the point where it barely feels worth keeping on my bars. - Please make Destruction nukes travel faster - Make Healthstones as good as potions. Healthstones aren't substitute health potions, health potions are substitute healthstones, just like Drums are substitute Bloodlust. Generic profession items should not supplant class utility. - Maybe make Havoc a bit more similar to Beacon of Light? Mouseover macros make using it pretty easy but the annoyance makes a lot of newbie warlocks ignore it. **In general** - Why did you ever remove Valor Points - Remove warlock tanking, then demon hunters? come on - Despite the heavily trimmed talent trees, talents still aren't balanced against each other - Many classes *need* their WoD tier bonuses to feel good to play
